"text": "Moapa Valley Water District\n Estimated Project      Recommendation\n Cost                   The Nevada Division of Environmental Protection (NDEP) recommends that the\n $1,267,300.00          Board for Financing Water Projects (Board) approve a Letter of Intent to fund Moapa\n                        Valley Water District for a capital improvement project for Supervisory Control and\n                        Data Acquisition (SCADA) improvements.\n Grant Percent          Resolution          Program and Terms\n\n 38                     G09-0826           Grant Funds\n\nManagement and Structure\n\n      Grant Recipient Moapa Valley Water District is a purveyor of water per NRS 349.980(10).\n       and Structure\n   System Number NV0000160\n\n\n\nSystem Information\n\n                  County Clark\n      System Population 8,500\n\n         System Service 2,623\n           Connections\n            Date System June 23, 1983\n               Founded\n System Infrastructure The system operates four active wells, chlorinators and treatment facilities, booster\n                       pumps and a distribution system.\n   System Compliance The system is currently in compliance with no outstanding violations or unresolved\n                     significant deficiencies.\n\n\n\nSystem Project for Funding\n\n DWSRF Priority Priority #121 on the Drinking Water SRF Priority List Effective May 2026.\n           List\n   System need The system currently operates a SCADA system that is more than 20 years old. The\n  for the project SCADA service provider that supports this legacy system is expected to discontinue\n                  operations within the next few years. Without a service provider the Moapa Valley Water\nPage 1 of 6                     Moapa Valley Water District                       August 2026",
